
os_learn stage shell
Buddy memory + callable processes + cooperative MLFQ
Type help for commands, or demo for a scheduling walkthrough.
os> help
help                         show commands
echo [words...]              print words
mem                          inspect buddy memory
alloc ORDER / free ID|all    allocate/release a tracked buddy block
ps / show PID                inspect processes and saved registers
queues                       inspect MLFQ queues and budgets
spawn cpu|yield|sleep [N]     create callable job (1..1024 steps)
run                          execute queued kernel jobs until idle
wake PID|all                 wake sleeping jobs
kill PID|all                 request termination; run to finish it
reap PID|all                 reclaim zombie resources
exit PID [CODE]              mark a non-running process exited
boost / tick [N]             boost priorities / advance test clock
image init|alt               create a saved user image
fork PID                     deep-copy a user-image process
exec PID init|alt [args...]   replace a saved user image
demo                         queue 3 CPU jobs and a sleeping job, then run
quit                         power off QEMU
Editing: backspace, Ctrl-U clear, Ctrl-C cancel, Ctrl-D quit.
User images support lifecycle inspection; run executes callable jobs.
